    "body": "# BetterTot 0.3.4\n\nBetterTot 0.3.4 tightens the scratchpad controls and keeps the website aligned\nwith the native app. Workspace and backup formats are unchanged.\n\n## Improvements\n\n- The scratchpad header is more compact, with smaller controls and pad dots.\n- The panel uses AppKit's native popover material for dark blurred transparency.\n- Light mode has clearer panel chrome and more distinct, readable pad colors.\n- The menu-bar icon shows an active state while the scratchpad is open.\n- Footer statistics stay on the left while list and Settings controls stay on\n  the right.\n- Command-B, Command-I, and Command-U apply portable Markdown-backed inline\n  formatting, including whole-line selections.\n- Storage actions have clearer separation from the latest backup details.\n- The website now renders its product demos in HTML and CSS, with corrected\n  menu-bar alignment and direct local asset loading.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- macOS 13 Ventura or later.\n- Apple silicon or Intel Mac. Release artifacts are universal `arm64` and\n  `x86_64` binaries.\n\n## Installation\n\nDownload `BetterTot-0.3.4.pkg` for the standard Installer flow, or extract\n`BetterTot-0.3.4.zip` and move `BetterTot.app` to `/Applications`. Verify both\nfiles against `BetterTot-0.3.4.sha256` before installation.\n\nThe app is ad-hoc signed, the installer is unsigned, and neither artifact is\nnotarized. After verifying the SHA-256 checksum, open the package normally. If\nmacOS blocks it, use **System Settings -> Privacy & Security -> Security -> Open\nAnyway**, authenticate, and confirm **Open**. Never disable Gatekeeper globally.\n\n## Upgrade Safety\n\nQuit BetterTot before upgrading. Pads, workspace metadata, preferences, and\niCloud backups live outside the application bundle and remain available after\nreplacing or reinstalling BetterTot.\n"
