    "body": "# BetterTot 0.3.3\n\nBetterTot 0.3.3 refines the scratchpad and Settings experience while keeping\nthe existing workspace and backup formats unchanged.\n\n## Improvements\n\n- The scratchpad uses a native blurred popover surface in light and dark\n  appearances.\n- Footer statistics use the compact `chars` label and can be hidden from\n  **Settings -> General -> Text Statistics**.\n- Settings command buttons use native Liquid Glass on macOS 26 or later and\n  retain standard rounded controls on earlier supported releases.\n- The iCloud backup summary is more compact, with backup actions grouped in\n  one place.\n- Pad name fields retain their standard editable background and border.\n- Pad name field styling remains consistent on macOS 13 through macOS 27.\n- Inline checkboxes align more consistently with editor text.\n- The README, website, and product demonstration have been refreshed to match\n  the current application.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- macOS 13 Ventura or later.\n- Apple silicon or Intel Mac. Release artifacts are universal `arm64` and\n  `x86_64` binaries.\n\n## Installation\n\nDownload `BetterTot-0.3.3.pkg` for the standard Installer flow, or extract\n`BetterTot-0.3.3.zip` and move `BetterTot.app` to `/Applications`. Verify both\nfiles against `BetterTot-0.3.3.sha256` before installation.\n\nThe app is ad-hoc signed, the installer is unsigned, and neither artifact is\nnotarized. After verifying the SHA-256 checksum, open the package normally. If\nmacOS blocks it, use **System Settings -> Privacy & Security -> Security -> Open\nAnyway**, authenticate, and confirm **Open**. Never disable Gatekeeper globally.\n\n## Upgrade Safety\n\nQuit BetterTot before upgrading. Pads, workspace metadata, preferences, and\niCloud backups live outside the application bundle and remain available after\nreplacing or reinstalling BetterTot.\n"
